# AWS Amplify Gen2 Backend Patterns for SPOTS

## Backend Architecture
- Use AWS Amplify Gen2 for backend infrastructure
- Configure auth, data, and API resources in [amplify/](mdc:spots-app/amplify) directory
- Main configuration in [amplify/backend.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/backend.ts)

## Authentication Configuration
- Reference [amplify/auth/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/auth/resource.ts) for auth setup
- Uses AWS Cognito with Google OAuth integration
- Supports email/password and Google sign-in
- Includes MFA support (optional TOTP)
- Configured callback URLs for localhost and production

## Cognito Username & REDCap Identity (Migration)
- **Sign-up users:** Username at sign-up must match REDCap `spots_user_id`; stored as Cognito `preferred_username` when allowed. REDCap lookup uses `getSpotsUserIdForValidation(session)` → `spots_user_id` in login API body.
- **Google users:** REDCap lookup uses email; login API still sends `spots_user_id` when available (from id token `preferred_username`), else email.
- **Login flow:** Always send `{ email, spots_user_id }` to `POST /api/auth/login`. See [app/_lib/services/auth/login-service.ts](app/_lib/services/auth/login-service.ts) (`getSpotsUserIdForValidation`, `performValidation`).

## Data Models
- Reference [amplify/data/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/data/resource.ts) for schema definition
- Uses Amplify Data for GraphQL API with DynamoDB
- Current models:
  - `User`: Extended user profile with role, name, timestamps
  - `Todo`: Example model (can be removed or repurposed)

### User Model Schema
```typescript
User: {
  email: string (required, unique identifier)
  role: string (default: 'user')
  givenName: string (optional)
  familyName: string (optional)
  createdAt: datetime
  updatedAt: datetime
}
```

## Authorization Patterns
- Owner-based authorization for user data
- Users can read, create, and update their own data
- Default authorization mode: "userPool"
- Extensible for admin roles and healthcare team access

## Frontend Integration
- Generate Data client using `generateClient<Schema>()`
- Use in client components with "use client" directive
- Example usage patterns in [amplify/data/resource.ts](mdc:spots-app/amplify/data/resource.ts) comments

## Development Workflow
- Use `amplify sandbox` for local development
- Deploy with `amplify push` for production
- Configure environment variables for OAuth secrets
- Test auth flows locally before deployment

## Security Considerations
- All user data is owner-protected
- OAuth secrets stored as Amplify secrets
- MFA available for enhanced security
- Follow healthcare data privacy requirements (HIPAA considerations)
